#!/bin/bash
# Set or clear the tab name override for the current terminal. Callable from
# any shell (zsh `tn` wraps this) OR from Claude Code's Bash tool — walks PPID
# up to find the controlling TTY in case the subprocess has no direct one.
#
# Usage:
#   tn <name>          PIN tab name (human). AI stops auto-renaming it.
#   tn --auto <name>   set name WITHOUT pinning (used by Claude's tab-name skill)
#   tn                 clear pin + override; auto-name (project basename) returns
#
# The colored status dot is painted separately by tab-watcher.sh and keeps
# updating regardless of the pin — only AI auto-renaming is suppressed.

state_dir="$HOME/.claude/terminal-state"
mkdir -p "$state_dir"

auto=0
if [ "$1" = "--auto" ]; then auto=1; shift; fi

pid=$$; tty_dev=""
for _ in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
  t=$(ps -o tty= -p "$pid" 2>/dev/null | tr -d ' ')
  if [ -n "$t" ] && [ "$t" != "??" ]; then
    tty_dev="$t"
    break
  fi
  pid=$(ps -o ppid= -p "$pid" 2>/dev/null | tr -d ' ')
  [ -z "$pid" ] && break
done

if [ -z "$tty_dev" ]; then
  echo "tn: no TTY" >&2
  exit 1
fi

# Target the live Claude session on this TTY (stable across TTY-number reuse by
# VS Code). Fall back to the legacy per-TTY file only for non-Claude shells.
sess=$(cat "$state_dir/tty.$tty_dev.session" 2>/dev/null)
if [ -n "$sess" ] && [ -f "$state_dir/$sess.state" ]; then
  target="$state_dir/$sess.name"; pin="$state_dir/$sess.pinned"; in_session=1
else
  target="$state_dir/tty.$tty_dev.name"; pin="$state_dir/tty.$tty_dev.pinned"; in_session=0
fi

if [ -z "$1" ]; then
  rm -f "$pin"
  if [ "$in_session" = 1 ]; then
    basename "$PWD" > "$target"   # restore auto-name (project basename)
  else
    rm -f "$target"
  fi
  echo "tn: cleared pin + override for $tty_dev"
else
  echo "$1" > "$target"
  if [ "$auto" = 1 ]; then
    echo "tn: tab → '$1' (auto, not pinned)"
  else
    touch "$pin"   # human pin → tab-name skill must not override
    echo "tn: tab → '$1' (pinned; AI will not rename)"
  fi
  # Only a live session has a watcher painting the title, so outside one this
  # wrote a file nobody reads. Say so instead of looking like it worked.
  if [ "$in_session" = 0 ]; then
    echo "tn: warning — no live Claude session on $tty_dev, so nothing is painting this tab" >&2
  fi
fi
